'''Aurê–Aurá''' is an extinct language, part of the [[Tupian language|Tupi language family]],<ref>
{{cite web |title=Aura Language and the Aurá Indian Tribe (Aure, Auras, Auré) |url=http://www.native-languages.org/aura.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816114820/http://www.native-languages.org/aura.htm |archive-date=16 August 2022 |access-date=2022-08-16}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Glottolog 4.6 - Aurê y Aurá |url=https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/aura1243 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816115618/https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/aura1243 |archive-date=16 August 2022 |access-date=2022-08-16}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite journal |last=Mello |first=Antonio Souza |date=1996 |title=Genetic affiliation of the language of the Indians Aurê and Aurá |url=https://produccioncientificaluz.org/index.php/opcion/article/download/6116/6105/ |journal=Opción: Revista de Ciencias Humanas y Sociales |volume=12 |issue=19 |pages=67–81}}</ref> last spoken by two individuals in [[Maranhão]], [[Brazil]] named Aurê and Aurá.<ref>
{{cite web |title=Sozinhos desde a infância, Aure e Aurá só conversam entre eles |url=http://www.letras.ufmg.br/lali/PDF/BANDEIRA,Luiza_aureaura.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816115722/http://www.letras.ufmg.br/lali/PDF/BANDEIRA,Luiza_aureaura.pdf |archive-date=16 August 2022 |access-date=2022-08-16}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2009 |title=Novo em Folha - Línguas ameaçadas de extinção no Brasil - Aurê-aurá |url=http://treinamento.folhasp.com.br/linguasdobrasil/lingua-aureaura.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160324225300/http://treinamento.folhasp.com.br/linguasdobrasil/lingua-aureaura.html |archive-date=2016-03-24 |access-date=2025-06-01 |website=Treinamento Folha}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Relatório de pesquisa linguística e antropológica com dois índios remanescentes, de grupo desconhecido, na região de Altamira, no Pará. {{!}} Acervo {{!}} ISA |url=https://acervo.socioambiental.org/index.php/acervo/documentos/relatorio-de-pesquisa-linguistica-e-antropologica-com-dois-indios-remanescentes |access-date=2025-06-01 |website=acervo.socioambiental.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=A questão Auré / Aurá. {{!}} Acervo {{!}} ISA |url=https://acervo.socioambiental.org/acervo/documentos/questao-aure-aura |access-date=2025-06-01 |website=acervo.socioambiental.org}}</ref> Both known speakers originally came from west of [[Marabá, Pará|Marabá]], [[Pará]]. The language primarily used [[nouns]], with few adjectives or verbs. Aurê died in 2014, leaving Aurá as the last known speaker of the language. Aurá died on September 20, 2025, at the age of 77, marking the definitive extinction of the language.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |date=2025-09-25 |title=Morre aos 77 anos Aurá, considerado último sobrevivente de povo indígena do MA |url=https://g1.globo.com/ma/maranhao/noticia/2025/09/25/morre-aos-77-anos-aura-considerado-ultimo-sobrevivente-de-povo-indigena-do-maranhao.ghtml |access-date=2025-09-26 |website=G1 |language=pt-br}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite web |date=2025-09-25 |title=Funai confirma morte de último indígena de etnia desconhecida |url=https://agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br/radioagencia-nacional/direitos-humanos/audio/2025-09/funai-confirma-morte-de-ultimo-indigena-de-etnia-desconhecida |access-date=2025-09-26 |website=Agência Brasil |language=pt-br}}</ref>

